#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A Python toolkit for randomization-based quantum noise characterization.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  **Alpha software.** This library is in the `0.x` stage of development and under active development. No part of the public interface is yet stable: while the major version is `0`, expect breaking changes between releases and pin your dependency accordingly (for example, `qiskit-noise-learning==0.1.*`). We do not currently issue deprecation warnings, but all changes are recorded in the [release notes](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/release-notes). See the [deprecation policy](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-noise-learning/blob/main/DEPRECATION.md) for details. All feedback is appreciated.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Interfaces and Documentation {#interfaces-and-documentation}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This library has two levels of interface. The first is the low-level "
"interface where the user directly interacts with objects representing core "
"concepts in noise learning, enabling custom design of every aspect of a "
"noise learning protocol. The second is a higher-level interface, the "
"`qiskit_noise_learning.protocols` subpackage, which holds one pair of "
"functions per protocol – `prepare_vanilla_program` and "
"`process_vanilla_result` for the standard “vanilla” protocol – each pair "
"wrapping a stock workflow into a single call on either side of execution.\n"
msgstr ""

